4). Describ the basic flutter app structure, explaining main.dart,the main functipon and the widget tree.

Ans :-A basic Flutter app is organized around a few core ideas: the entry point (main.dart),the main() function, and the widget tree. 

      Understanding these gives you a clear mental model of how Flutter builds UI.

        1. main.dart (the entry file) :

          -> main.dart is the starting file of a Flutter app, usually located in the lib/ folder. 

          -> It contains the code that launches your application and defines the root widget.

          -> Think of it as the “front door” of your app. When the app starts, Flutter looks here first.

             A very simple example:

            import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

            void main() {
                         runApp(MyApp());
                        }

        2. main() function :

          ->the main function is Starting point of app it Calls runApp().
        
             It is the first thing that runs when your app starts.

             Every Dart program must have it.

        3. Widget Tree :

            -> Flutter doesn’t use buttons, screens, layouts separately like other frameworks.
  
               In flutter Everything is a widget.

                  It’s just a structure of widgets inside widgets.

                  Like:
    
                  One widget contains another
                  That one contains another
                  And so on…

                     
                 MaterialApp
                  └── Scaffold
                     ├── AppBar
                     │    └── Text("My First App")
                     └── Center
                          └── Text("Hello, Flutter!")

                   
                 
               
                    
                    
